Fictional EP Tracklist

Track 1: Delivery Refused at the Crossing
- Story & Context: Silas Vance salvaged a box of uncollected 1970s freight manifests from the depot in Altoona, discovering a series of frantic hand-written notes stamped return to sender. He mapped the rhythmic cadence of the stamped dates into a sequence on his pocket sampler while riding the 2:00 AM express through a torrential thunderstorm. The track captures the exact moment the train locked brakes near an unmapped junction, featuring a howling slide guitar hook that cuts through heavy 808 sub-slides. Over a stuttering drill hi-hat, Vance mutters the hook, "Stamped your address on a burning engine, but the mail car cleared the track."
