Track 2: [60100] Return to Sender
- Story & Context: Recorded in the reverberating steel stairwell of the Scranton postal sorting facility, Mara O'Shea routed her slide guitar through a broken tape delay to imitate the mechanical clatter of automated sorters. The song acts as a quiet confession regarding a long-lost sister whose final postcard was lost between regional zip codes during the winter of 2021. The tension peaks as ambient train-whistle pitch-bends collide with rapid-fire 2020s drill snare rolls and heavy sub-frequencies. O'Shea’s faint, double-tracked vocal whispers the central line: "Six digits inked upon my palm, but your ghost don't take no mail."
