Track 3: The Mail Car Screams at 4 AM
- Story & Context: Scene mythology claims this final track was bounced directly to cassette during a high-speed police chase along the rail corridor outside Cleveland. Local commuters tuned their car radios to 88.7 FM to hear O'Shea's lap steel bending like a siren over explosive, distorted bass drops and industrial metal scrapes. The track abruptly cuts to pure field recording ambient noise, leaving only the sound of wind rushing through an open freight door. Vance closes the EP's arc with the haunting lyric, "When the engine stops, the rust remains, reading words we never sent."
